WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.140
The Witcher features a stellar cast, and there’s
no doubt that fans have recognized some of

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:09.680
the show's phenomenal actors but, despite
their best efforts, can't quite place them.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:14.220
So let's glance over these performers' past
accomplishments and figure out why the cast

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.200
of The Witcher looks so familiar.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:21.180
Monster hunter Geralt of Rivia is portrayed
by Henry Cavill, easily the most recognizable

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.360
member of the cast.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.340
"How do you like my eyes?"

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:30.440
Cavill began his career in 2001, and he earned
worldwide fame by playing the darkest live-action

00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:36.390
version of Superman to date, showing up in
DCEU films like Man of Steel and Batman v

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:37.620
Superman: Dawn of Justice.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.360
You might also know him from Mission: Impossible,
Fallout and from Showtime's The Tudors.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:47.060
Fantasy fans might also recognize him from
his smaller roles in films like Stardust and

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:52.070
Tristan &amp; Isolde, proving that he can hold
his own in a fairy and dragon-infested setting

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.560
just as well as on Krypton.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:58.559
In fact, Cavill admits to loving Andrzej Sapowski's
original Witcher novels and to being a big

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.880
fan of fantasy since he was very young.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.680
Freya Allan was tapped to play Princess Cirilla,
aka Ciri, an on-the-run royal with mysterious,

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:07.760
frightening powers.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:12.280
Allan herself, though not quite as young as
Ciri, is still fairly new to Hollywood, a

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:15.340
fresh face who's proven she has what it takes
to have a long career.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:20.020
Immediately prior to The Witcher, she had
a small role in a BBC mini-series adaptation

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:23.820
of The War of the Worlds, and she also briefly
showed up Into the Badlands.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:28.799
Like the young cast of Stranger Things, Allan's
Netflix debut is sure to snag her more work

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.960
both within the streaming service's original
content, as well as in film.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.100
"Who is Yennefer?"

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:40.740
Anya Chalotra, aka the sorceress Yennefer,
is fairly new to screen acting.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:46.020
Her breakout role was in the BBC's Wanderlust,
followed by a small part in The ABC Murders.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:50.520
She's also lent her vocal talents as the lead
part of Robin Loxley in the futuristic animated

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:51.680
series Sherwood.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.579
And with such a stunning performance as the
witch who wants it all, it will be a pleasure

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:59.280
to see Chalotra continue on to more prominent
roles going forward.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:04.160
Yennefer would never have been able to harness
her powers if not for the influence of Tissaia,

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:05.680
the head of a magical academy.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:09.360
Typically, a character like this would be
played as a hateful stepmother stereotype,

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:15.040
but in the very capable hands of MyAnna Buring,
Tissaia is as complex, intriguing, and sympathetic

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:17.100
a character as Yennefer herself.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.920
As for Buring, her first super visible role
was as Tanya in both parts of The Twilight

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:22.920
Saga: Breaking Dawn.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:26.520
Her stately manner then graced the set of
Downton Abbey as Edna.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:31.840
Actor Joey Batey brings plenty of plucky charm
and a soothing singing voice to the character

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:36.600
of Jaskier, the bard who takes up with Geralt,
much to the gruff witcher's dismay.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:41.340
Before taking up the lute, Batey had small
roles in several television series, including

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:45.260
The White Queen, another series featuring
strong-willed and powerful women.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:50.060
Lovers of historical dramas might also recognize
him from his recurring role as Pierre on the

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.740
History Channel's Knightfall.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:55.440
The Witcher boasts a cast of extremely powerful
and influential women.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.900
And it's hard to get much more powerful and
influential than Calanthe, warrior queen of

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:00.700
Cintra.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:05.680
Calanthe is brought to life by the incomparable
Jodhi May, who's no stranger to playing a

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:09.720
queen, having taken up the mantle of Queen
Victoria in The Warrior Queen of Jhansi.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:14.780
She appeared in an episode of Game of Thrones
in 2015 as a fortune teller named Maggy, a

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:18.939
small role but interesting to note considering
how much The Witcher has been compared to

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.520
the HBO fantasy series.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:25.460
You might also recognize her from her role
as Alice Munro in the 1992 adaptation of The

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:28.540
Last of the Mohicans, starring Daniel Day-Lewis.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.580
Ah, the mage with the amusing name.

00:03:30.599 --> 00:03:35.709
Mousesack is portrayed by Adam Levy, perhaps
recognizable to superhero fans from his one-off

00:03:35.709 --> 00:03:39.660
role as an alien healer named Amadei in the
Supergirl TV series.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.760
Fans of Hallmark Christmas movies may have
spotted him in 2018's A Christmas in Royal

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:44.500
Fashion.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.700
He's also been part of his fair share of historical
dramas, including A.D.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.900
The Bible Continues and Knightfall with Joey
Batey.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:57.240
To play the conniving mage Stregobor, the
showrunners cast Danish actor Lars Mikkelsen,

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.180
the brother of Hannibal's Mads Mikkelsen.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:03.100
Unless you're very familiar with Danish film
and television, it's unlikely you've seen

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:03.920
a lot of him.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:08.160
However, he played the recurring character
Viktor Petrov in the very popular Netflix

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:13.999
series House of Cards, and fans of BBC's Sherlock
will easily recognize him as Charles Magnussen

00:04:13.999 --> 00:04:16.880
from the episodes "His Last Vow" and "The
Empty Hearse."

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:21.099
It seems Mikkelsen has a knack for playing
sinister types, and his casting as Stregobor

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.700
is spot-on in this regard.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:27.600
The rightful heir of the Nilfgaardian throne,
Cahir is a violent, ambitious prince who's

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.980
single-mindedly pursuing Ciri to use her mysterious
powers for his own ends.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:36.440
Cahir is portrayed by Eamon Farren, notable
for his appearance as Richard Horne on the

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:39.100
most recent season of David Lynch's Twin Peaks.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:43.700
He also had a recurring role in the first
three episodes of BBC's adaptation of Agatha

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:48.150
Christie's The ABC Murders, which featured
an appearance by The Witcher co-star Anya

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.220
Chalotra, as well.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:54.180
He also had a role in the eerie drama Winchester,
about a maze-like mansion and its strange

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:55.740
owner, played by Helen Mirren.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:01.000
Dara is played by the young but very talented
Wilson Radjou-Pujalte, who's had roles in

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.200
several lesser-known television series.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.940
His largest role is easily that of Aladdin
in the BBC series Jamillah and Aladdin.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.800
He also has a substantial part in the Nickelodeon
series Hunter Street.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:16.060
And like many British actors, he's found work
in a Charles Dickens-inspired series.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:19.740
In this case, he starred as Dodger in BBC's
Dickensian.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:24.480
Triss Merigold initially seems like a one-off
character whose purpose is to hire Geralt

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:25.920
to slay a horrible monster.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:29.380
Instead, she becomes a more prominent player
later in the series.

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:33.740
Triss is played by Anna Shaffer, who kicked
off her acting career in a rather impressive

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:38.060
way, playing Romilda Vane in Harry Potter
and the Half-Blood Prince and Harry Potter

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:39.360
and the Deathly Hallows.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:43.860
She was also on the British teen soap opera
Hollyoaks for seven years as Ruby Button,

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:47.740
her stint there spanning an impressive 242
episodes.

